###Question: In the management of blood transfusion complication:
###Options:
A.  a.	Antihistamine is indicated in febrile transfusion complication;
B.  b.	Transfusion is always discontinued in febrile transfusion complication;
C.  c.	Slowing the rate of transfusion is helpful in haemolytic transfusion complication;
D.  d.	Diuretic may be indicated;
E.  e.	High dose immunoglobulin may be indicated.

###Answer:

outputs:
 A. a. Antihistamine is indicated in febrile transfusion complication;
D. d. Diuretic may be indicated.
###Explanation: In the management of blood transfusion complications, antihistamines are indicated in febrile transfusion complications. This is because allergic reactions, which are the typical cause of fever following a transfusion, respond well to antihistamines, which help to reduce itching and fever. Diuretics may also be indicated, particularly in cases of volume overload or congestive heart failure, which can occur rarely during transfusion.

